    "_comment": "Canonical marketing chrome: the top mega nav and the footer link lists. The header and footer are separate lists on purpose: the header carries the primary tasks, each page once; the footer carries utility, trust and company links plus long-tail pages the header leaves out, and is not a copy of the mega nav. components/AppHeader.vue and components/AppFooter.vue import this file directly. Icon keys are filenames in nuxt/assets/nav-icons/; utils/navIcons.ts resolves them, and a unit test keeps the two in sync. Class strings are literal so Tailwind can see them (assets/css/style.css and assets/css/theme.css each declare an @source for this file). An href of 'site:<key>' is resolved against nuxt/data/site.json at render time instead of being a literal URL, so values like the job board link stay single-sourced there.",
